Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 05:25:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] anv: run on macOS over xemac, a kernel extension speaking
 the xe uAPI

-Dxemac=<dir> points at the user-space side of a macOS kernel extension
that implements Linux's xe uAPI (DRM core syncobj ioctls plus DRM_XE_*)
behind an IOUserClient: xemac.h/xemac.c and a libdrm stand-in
(libdrm/xf86drm.h, xemac_drm.c) that implements the libdrm calls Mesa
makes on top of xemac_ioctl(). With it:

- dep_libdrm is the stand-in, so HAVE_LIBDRM code (vk_drm_syncobj,
  u_sync_provider, vk_instance's DRM enumeration, intel_kmd,
  intel_device_info) builds and runs unchanged;
- intel_ioctl() goes to xemac_ioctl(), like intel_virtio_ioctl() for
  virtio;
- anv opens and closes its device through anv_kmd_open()/anv_kmd_close()
  (xemac_open()/xemac_close()), and xe BO maps go through xemac_mmap()/
  xemac_munmap(), since IOKit mappings must be torn down by the kernel
  extension;
- dma-buf/sync_file/opaque fd sharing and VK_EXT_physical_device_drm are
  not advertised.

Generated-by: LLM
